## Overview

A senior student from a linguistics high school (*liceo linguistico*) is preparing to enroll in a university degree in **mathematics, physics, or engineering**. Linguistics high schools typically allocate limited curriculum time to trigonometry, limits, and derivatives. Therefore, the main challenge is not just missing calculus topics, but ensuring **algebraic fluency and mathematical rigor** upon which university courses immediately build.

This series of pages serves as the log of our journey: what we cover, in what order, what works, and what needs adjustment. The primary reference material is the open-source book
[Mathematics for High Schools](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/intro.html) (Jupyter Book), which is refined and completed as needed.

::: {.callout-note}
## Privacy
The tutoring process is described anonymously, with the student's consent. This blog focuses on methodology and materials rather than personal details.
:::

<!--
## How It Works

The program is **remote and partially asynchronous**:

1. Before each session, the student receives a worksheet (reading + exercises) on a specific topic to tackle independently, noting down any roadblocks.
2. We hold a weekly online session (about 60 minutes) dedicated to clarifying doubts, reviewing solutions, and working through exercises together. During more challenging blocks, a second shorter practice session is added.
3. At the end of each block, a short quiz (8–10 exercises) helps decide whether a review is necessary.
4. After each session, a log entry is added to [this page](#session-log).
-->

## Topics & Curriculum

| # | Block | What is Learned | Book Chapters |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Diagnostics | Baseline assessment and gap identification | — |
| 1 | Functions & Analytic Geometry | Cartesian plane, lines, conics, concept of function, domain, and graphs | [12](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/analytic_geometry/analytic_geometry_2d.html), [15](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/precalculus/real-functions.html) |
| 2 | Vectors | Position vectors, components, scalar product, and physical applications | [7](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/algebra/vector-algebra.html) |
| 3 | Advanced Algebra | Powers, roots, polynomials, equations, and inequalities | [4](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/algebra/real-algebra.html), [20](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/precalculus/polynomials.html) |
| 4 | Exponential & Logarithm | Properties, graphs, and logarithmic/exponential equations | [19](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/precalculus/exponential_logarithm.html) |
| 5 | Trigonometry | Unit circle, trigonometric identities, equations, and inequalities | [18](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/trigonometry.html) |
| 6 | Limits & Continuity | Limits, indeterminate forms, asymptotes | [24](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/infinitesimal_calculus/analysis.html) |
| 7 | Derivatives | Definition, rules, curve sketching | [25](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/infinitesimal_calculus/derivatives.html) |
| 8 | Integrals & Complex Numbers (Preview) | Antiderivatives, definite integrals, complex numbers | [26](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/infinitesimal_calculus/integrals.html), [22](https://basics2022.github.io/bbooks-math-miscellanea-hs/ch/algebra/complex-algebra.html) |

After block 5, the path can diverge: more proofs and theoretical rigor for mathematics and physics, or more practical computation and vector calculus for engineering.

